`mfetch` also allows you to check whether you have modified any of the
source
files (for a bug fix) or to generate a `*.locked` file so that you can then
verify the reproducibility of your unikernel using our other tool
[`orb`][orb].
The tool itself is not revolutionary, but it helps to streamline the
workflow.

```shell
$ mfetch status
digestif                         ok
mkernel                          ok
$ mfetch lock
